EU. Global Ship Lease, Inc. was founded in 2007 and is based in Athens, Greece.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas A. Lister | Chief Executive Officer | Age 55","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7 people. Revenue per employee of $109.5M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $73.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2.0M per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Global Ship Lease Inc New is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $766M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $514M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 67 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 5.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 48% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 83% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 72% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dividend Raise Might Change The Case For Investing In Global Ship Lease Stock (GSL)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/transportation/nyse-gsl/global-ship-lease/news/dividend-raise-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-global","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794446875.358,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (GSL) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_